"""
Wallpaper Gallery  (v5)
───────────────────────
• Reads wallpapers from the Windows default wallpaper folder
  (%USERPROFILE%\\Pictures and the system Themes/wallpaper folder).
• Uses ctypes / windows APIs to set the desktop wallpaper.
• Parallelogram carousel: cards shrink linearly toward the edges,
  stop shrinking after position 7, no opacity dimming on side cards,
  outline glows on hover.
• Applying a wallpaper:
    1. The gallery starts fading out the moment a wallpaper is selected
       (double-click), so the desktop is visible while the change plays.
    2. A diagonal wipe plays: the new image sweeps in from the top-right
       corner to the bottom-left corner (duration set by REVEAL_WIPE_MS).
       The reveal window is reparented into the desktop's own WorkerW
       layer (the same trick live-wallpaper tools use), so it renders
       underneath every open application window and underneath the
       desktop icons, above only the true static wallpaper.
    3. When the wipe finishes, the real wallpaper is set on a background
       thread (so nothing freezes). The reveal image stays on screen for
       REVEAL_HOLD_MS after Windows reports the change, so the desktop
       never shows a blank gap while Windows swaps its own wallpaper.
    4. The reveal then fades away and ONLY THEN does the app exit: it
       quits once the gallery has faded out, the wipe has finished, the
       wallpaper has been applied and the reveal image is gone.
• Toolbar: ALL | PIC | VID | WE | 🗓 | 🎨 [swatches] | ♥ | ↓ | ⚙ | total | fav

Performance notes (perf pass):
  - Thumbnails are cached once as a downscaled "master" pixmap sized to
    the largest card (the centre card). All per-frame scaling during the
    slide animation happens off this small master.
  - While a slide animation is in flight, cards render with fast
    (nearest-neighbour) scaling and antialiasing off; once the slide
    settles, `_rebuild()` snaps everything back to smooth rendering.
  - The device pixel ratio is resolved once at startup.

Thumbnail loading pass:
  - Thumbnails are loaded off the GUI thread on a QThreadPool, with a
    persistent on-disk cache (small pre-scaled JPEGs).
  - A card shows an immediate placeholder the instant it's needed, and
    swaps in the real image the moment the background load finishes.
  - Loads are prioritized outward from the centre card.

All-cards pass:
  - EVERY wallpaper is a card. There is no longer a fixed pool of 47
    cards, so nothing is missing or blank no matter how fast or how far
    you scroll.
  - The strip is virtualized: the carousel keeps one float scroll
    position and only realises widgets for the cards that are actually
    on screen (a few dozen), recycling them as you scroll. Cost per frame
    no longer depends on library size.
  - Thumbnail masters are center-cropped to the widest region any card
    can show (instead of the full image), which looks identical but uses
    ~3.5x less memory, and are kept at the tallest card's full physical
    resolution. The in-memory cache is an LRU with a byte budget; evicted
    thumbnails come straight back from the small on-disk cache.
  - Only a window of thumbnails around the centre is prefetched, not the
    whole library, on a dedicated pool so decoding never starves the GUI.
"""

